From d9962f155a71d6fb86265981cc78115c931bf5a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:23:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] fix(replace job): search for the gap's size when
 nothing fits; a model URL never 404s; "next one" with nothing in the gap
 places one

Live on :8005, "the fridge is too small for us, get us a bigger one" (Grok: replace_component,
query "bigger fridge") found 36-60 in fridges for the kitchen's 80 cm fridge gap (x1.63) and
stopped. Now:
- When nothing that came back fits or is tight, the job searches once more for parts of the
  gap's size: the widest standard width of the kind that fits it ("30 inch fridge"; replace.sized_query,
  PRIORS widths_in), and uses those when one fits.
- The plain kind's fallback search starts only when the named search is slow (45 s) or comes back
  empty, not alongside every named search (SerpApi quota).
- GET /parts/{id}/model.glb builds a searched part's model on first request (assets.resolve_shared,
  90 s cap, 504 past it) instead of a 404 while the background worker hasn't got to it.
- "next one" / "option 2" / "put it in" swap (cycle_model) only when a model stands in the gap;
  otherwise place_part (after a job that stopped at the pick, nothing is there).

